            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioner, petitioner states that when a prisoner wins a civil rights case and is awarded damages and attorney\u2019s fees, the prisoner must pay part of the fees out of the judgment."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioner",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "46b45685fd88070bd31b3e398f249e70a5f51ecd1d0637208e004cad7ab443b0",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-46b45685fd88-0000-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 16,
              "start": 16
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioner, the statute at issue limits the prisoner\u2019s share of attorney\u2019s fees to not exceed 25\u202fpercent of the judgment, with any amount above that to be paid by the defendant."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioner",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "46b45685fd88070bd31b3e398f249e70a5f51ecd1d0637208e004cad7ab443b0",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-46b45685fd88-0000-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 14,
              "start": 14
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioner, district courts consider how the allocation of fees may deter future misconduct by prison guards and discourage prisoners with valid claims from filing suit."
      }
    ],
